{"id": "EUVD-2020-31283", "enisaUuid": "b6c568d5-9f06-3753-af11-12c433d3f2b8", "description": "Vyper before 0.2.6 contains a call stack corruption vulnerability that causes incorrect function outputs when complex types with non-base members are passed as arguments. Contracts passing multi-dimensional arrays or structs to internal or external functions receive corrupted values because the compiler assumed each subtype size is 32.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T00:36:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T00:36:16", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/security/advisories/GHSA-4v7v-gqf9-ww2g", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/vyper-before-0.2.6-call-stack-corruption-via-complex-type-function-arguments"], "aliases": ["CVE-2020-37287", "GHSA-cqxq-3fq9-6g4p"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5e5e442f-fa71-3db7-839c-c81d8e912c3e", "product": {"name": "vyper", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.2.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "736edbfa-bc1f-3e69-ba8d-7ff74edbd5e9", "vendor": {"name": "vyperlang"}}], "isExploited": false}